hundred years is a long time,

00:28:09.430 --> 00:28:12.091
why haven't we been able to get to know

00:28:12.091 --> 00:28:14.017
more than ten percent of the brain?

00:28:14.017 --> 00:28:15.900
12 percent, 15 percent, 20 percent?

00:28:15.900 --> 00:28:16.733
- Two reasons.

00:28:16.733 --> 00:28:21.150
It's hard to study the thing
that is giving you the thoughts

00:28:21.150 --> 00:28:22.670
to study the thing.

00:28:22.670 --> 00:28:23.741
- Oh.

00:28:23.741 --> 00:28:25.397
- It's very recursive, right?

00:28:25.397 --> 00:28:27.223
- You just blew my mind, man.

00:28:29.200 --> 00:28:30.330
- You want to hear another recursive-

00:28:30.330 --> 00:28:31.940
Recursion is very mind-blowing.

00:28:31.940 --> 00:28:33.760
You ready? Because I recently got a word

00:28:33.760 --> 00:28:35.249
into the Oxford English Dictionary.

00:28:35.249 --> 00:28:36.082
- Did you really?

00:28:36.082 --> 00:28:36.915
- Did you know about that?
- No!

00:28:36.915 --> 00:28:37.748
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:28:37.748 --> 00:28:39.090
The Manhattanhenge was in there.

00:28:39.090 --> 00:28:41.820
It says, "First used
by Neil Tyson in 2003."

00:28:41.820 --> 00:28:43.090
I said, "What took you so long?

00:28:43.090 --> 00:28:44.805
16 years later, but I'll take it."

00:28:44.805 --> 00:28:45.816
- That's the word again?

00:28:45.816 --> 00:28:46.935
- Manhattanhenge.

00:28:46.935 --> 00:28:47.800
You know, Manhattanhenge.

00:28:47.800 --> 00:28:48.633
- Oh?

00:28:48.633 --> 00:28:49.466
- Those are the two days of the year

00:28:49.466 --> 00:28:51.450
the sunset aligns on the Manhattan grid,

00:28:51.450 --> 00:28:53.410
and now thousands of
people flood the streets

00:28:53.410 --> 00:28:54.243
blocking traffic.

00:28:54.243 --> 00:28:55.141
It's great.

00:28:55.141 --> 00:28:55.974
- Oh my gosh.

00:28:55.974 --> 00:28:57.330
- Think about all the other reasons

00:28:57.330 --> 00:28:58.560
traffic had been blocked.

00:28:58.560 --> 00:29:00.210
