00:30:04.240 --> 00:30:05.077
(laughs)

00:30:05.077 --> 00:30:08.010
"Oh you're so smart
Oxford Dictionary People.

00:30:08.010 --> 00:30:08.843
Ooh!"

00:30:08.843 --> 00:30:09.676
- I didn't say they succeed at this,

00:30:09.676 --> 00:30:11.310
I'm saying this is
their mission statement,

00:30:11.310 --> 00:30:14.640
to have every usage over every word

00:30:15.870 --> 00:30:17.390
ever

00:30:17.390 --> 00:30:18.590
in the English language.

00:30:19.490 --> 00:30:21.230
So if a word first appears,

00:30:21.230 --> 00:30:22.870
they have the first
appearance of that word.

00:30:22.870 --> 00:30:25.190
If you use that word slightly differently,

00:30:25.190 --> 00:30:26.560
pivoting its definition,

00:30:26.560 --> 00:30:29.733
that usage is then given.
- Oh wow, I didn't know.

00:30:29.733 --> 00:30:31.266
- [Neil] If you pivot
it again, it's gonna-

00:30:31.266 --> 00:30:32.099
There it is.

00:30:32.099 --> 00:30:33.033
- And this gets back to
the point about the brain,

00:30:33.033 --> 00:30:34.597
because the brain,

00:30:34.597 --> 00:30:35.880
we can get only to ten percent,

00:30:35.880 --> 00:30:37.900
because the thoughts that you need--

00:30:37.900 --> 00:30:39.503
- No, no, forget the ten percent.

00:30:39.503 --> 00:30:41.190
It was misinformation
from the very beginning.

00:30:41.190 --> 00:30:42.023
- No I understand that,

00:30:42.023 --> 00:30:43.450
but when I asked well why can't we,

00:30:43.450 --> 00:30:45.385
with all this advancement--
- Well one of the challenges,

00:30:45.385 --> 00:30:46.784
how do you study the thing

00:30:46.784 --> 00:30:47.617
that is the thing that's
studying the thing?

00:30:50.450 --> 00:30:51.283
A.

00:30:51.283 --> 00:30:54.730
B: You can't just sit
